        "options": [
          {
            "id": "graph-a",
            "text": "The graph is the full straight line through $(0,6)$ and $(4,0)$, extending in both directions. It also contains $(-2,9)$, $(2,3)$, and $(6,-3)$.\n\nIts points lie in quadrant II for $x<0$, in I for $0<x<4$, and in IV for $x>4$. It has no points in III. At $x=0$ and $x=4$, its points are on the axes.",
